{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.WeilZeta","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.WeilZeta","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.LocalQZetaFunction","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Pow.Real","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Pow.NNReal","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Polynomial.Roots"],"declarations":10,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.instIsWeilZetaWeilZetaExample","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.instIsWeilZetaWeilZetaExample","kind":"instance","line":169,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/WeilZeta.lean#L169-L174","doc":"The example is a Weil datum, so `IsWeilZeta` is inhabited and its two\nfields are jointly consistent — unlike the global axioms it replaces. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.weilZetaExample","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.weilZetaExample","kind":"def","line":157,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/WeilZeta.lean#L157-L167","doc":"A concrete `LocalQZetaFunction` with `q = 4` and all eigenvalues `2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.hasse_weil_bound","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.hasse_weil_bound","kind":"theorem","line":124,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/WeilZeta.lean#L124-L146","doc":"**Hasse–Weil bound**: every fundamental Frobenius eigenvalue αᵢ\nof Bring's curve satisfies |αᵢ| = q^{1/2}.\n\nThis is the Riemann hypothesis for curves over finite fields,\nproved by Weil via the Castelnuovo–Severi inequality on the\nself-product B × B.\n\nStated **conditionally on `[IsWeilZeta Z]`** (§3b-cond): the two Weil\ninputs are hypotheses, and everything else is derived. The proof combines:\n- `eigenvalue_functional_equation` (symmetry of the zeta function)\n- `castelnuovo_severi_bound` (Hodge index theorem on B × B)\n- `eigenvalue_norm_sq` (combining the two forces equality) ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:thm:hasse-weil-bound","label":"thm:hasse-weil-bound","md":"quantum-observable-universe/q-geometric-langlands/hasse-weil-bound.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.eigenvalue_norm_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.eigenvalue_norm_sq","kind":"theorem","line":97,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/WeilZeta.lean#L97-L122","doc":"The functional equation + Castelnuovo–Severi together force\n|αᵢ|² = q (not just ≤).\n\nThe functional equation gives |αᵢ| · |q/αᵢ| = q for paired\neigenvalues, so |αᵢ|² ≥ q. Combined with CS, equality holds.\nSee [rosen2002] Ch 5, proof of Thm 5.12.\n\nThis step is *derived*, not assumed: it is the one piece of the Hasse–Weil\nargument the corpus proves itself. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.castelnuovo_severi_bound","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.castelnuovo_severi_bound","kind":"theorem","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/WeilZeta.lean#L89-L95","doc":"The Castelnuovo–Severi inequality on B × B bounds the\nself-intersection of the Frobenius correspondence, yielding\n|αᵢ|² ≤ q for all i. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.eigenvalue_functional_equation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.eigenvalue_functional_equation","kind":"theorem","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/WeilZeta.lean#L80-L87","doc":"The functional equation of the local zeta function constrains\neigenvalue norms: if αᵢ is an eigenvalue, so is q/αᵢ.\nThis pairs eigenvalues such that |αᵢ| · |q/αᵢ| = q. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.IsWeilZeta.castelnuovo_severi","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.IsWeilZeta.castelnuovo_severi","kind":"theorem","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/WeilZeta.lean#L78-L78","doc":"Castelnuovo–Severi: `|αᵢ|² ≤ q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.IsWeilZeta.functional_equation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.IsWeilZeta.functional_equation","kind":"theorem","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/WeilZeta.lean#L74-L74","doc":"Functional-equation pairing: `αᵢ ↦ q/αᵢ` **permutes** the eigenvalues.\n\nStated as a permutation rather than as `∀ i, ∃ j`. The existential form is\nstrictly weaker and loses multiplicities — it is satisfied by families in\nwhich two eigenvalues share a partner and a third has none — so nothing\nabout the root *multiset* follows from it, and `charPoly_map_conj` below\nis exactly such a multiset statement. Weil's functional equation does\nsupply the bijection, so this is the faithful form, not a strengthening\nof the cited result. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.IsWeilZeta.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.IsWeilZeta.mk","kind":"ctor","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/WeilZeta.lean#L64-L64","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.IsWeilZeta","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.IsWeilZeta","kind":"class","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/WeilZeta.lean#L46-L78","doc":"**Weil datum.** The hypothesis that `Z` is the zeta function of a smooth\nprojective geometrically irreducible curve over `𝔽_q`, recorded through the\ntwo consequences the Hasse–Weil argument consumes.\n\nBoth fields are classical theorems *about such curves*, not properties of an\narbitrary `LocalQZetaFunction` — see the module docstring for the `False`\nderivations that follow from asserting them universally.\n\n* `functional_equation` — the functional equation of the zeta function of a\n  curve pairs each eigenvalue `αᵢ` with `q/αᵢ`.\n  See [weil1948] §IV, or [rosen2002] Ch 5, Thm 5.9.\n* `castelnuovo_severi` — the Castelnuovo–Severi inequality on `B × B`\n  (Hodge index theorem) bounds the self-intersection of the Frobenius\n  correspondence, giving `|αᵢ|² ≤ q`.\n  See [weil1948] §V; [milne2013] §27; [rosen2002] Ch 5, Thm 5.10. ","signatureChunk":0}]}